  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "A polynomial \\(p(x)\\) has remainder three when divided by \\(x-1\\) and remainder five when divided by \\(x-3.\\) The remainder when \\(p(x)\\) is divided by \\((x-1)(x-3)\\) is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(x-2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(x+2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(8\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(15\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1976-p19.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the remainder be \\(r(x)=ax+b.\\) Since \\(p(1)=3\\) and \\(p(3)=5,\\) we have \\(a+b=3,\\) and \\(3a+b=5.\\) Thus \\(a=1,\\) and \\(b=2,\\) so the remainder is \\(x+2.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "The desired remainder has degree less than two, so write it as \\(ax+b\\)",
        "Use the remainder theorem at \\(x=1\\) and \\(x=3\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
